     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Hello, </div><div><br></div><div>A few months ago I used the Distance package in R to conduct distance sampling for a dataset and did not see any warnings or errors. </div><div><br></div><div>This week I am trying to run the same analysis with updated distance values (~10% coerced to a value of 0), and I am getting various warnings and errors from the ds() and gof_ds functions. I would like to understand if this is a result of the values/ distribution of the distance values in my data, or an issue in R that I could resolve. </div><div><br></div><div>If anyone recognizes any of these warnings/ errors and has advice please let me know.</div><div><br></div><div>Thanks,</div><div>Annabel </div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>Depending on the inputs for ds(), gof_ds() sometimes produces this warning: </div><div><br></div><div><img src=\"https://groups.google.com/group/distance-sampling/attach/496f855e59be5/Screen%20Shot%202021-11-22%20at%205.45.36%20PM.png?part=0.1&amp;view=1\" alt=\"Screen Shot 2021-11-22 at 5.45.36 PM.png\" width=\"511\" height=\"211\" style=\"outline:0px\"><br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>Depending on the adjustment inputs, ds() produces various warnings/ errors. </div><div><br></div><img src=\"https://groups.google.com/group/distance-sampling/attach/496f855e59be5/Screen%20Shot%202021-11-22%20at%205.46.27%20PM.png?part=0.5&amp;view=1\" alt=\"Screen Shot 2021-11-22 at 5.46.27 PM.png\" width=\"511\" height=\"62\"><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><img src=\"https://groups.google.com/group/distance-sampling/attach/496f855e59be5/Screen%20Shot%202021-11-22%20at%205.47.26%20PM.png?part=0.6&amp;view=1\" alt=\"Screen Shot 2021-11-22 at 5.47.26 PM.png\" width=\"511\" height=\"169\" style=\"outline:0px\"></div><div><br></div><div><br><div><img src=\"https://groups.google.com/group/distance-sampling/attach/496f855e59be5/Screen%20Shot%202021-11-22%20at%205.47.48%20PM.png?part=0.2&amp;view=1\" alt=\"Screen